===Alternative spellings===
* [[oyes]]

===Etymology===
{{L.}} ''audire'' to hear; through Old French ''ouïr'' to hear; through Anglo-French.

===Interjection===
{{infl|en|interjection}}

# Hear ye. Attend. (Called by public [[crier]]s or in [[court]] usually three times to secure silence).

====Usage notes====
* Practise note: It is still used in the United States Supreme Court, and in many state supreme courts, although lower courts seem to have dropped its use.

